=== REASONING ===

Why this design preserves ADR-015 + P1–P10 + the non-AI baseline:

P1 (provider port): the strategy returns a system-prompt + tool
whitelist; the handler resolves a *provider.Provider via
*provider.Registry.For per request. No direct provider-adapter
import — the strategy and handler are decoupled from the cloud /
local adapter implementations.

P2 (settings shape): the registry entry sets DefaultOn=false, so
the feature is opt-in. The guard reads ai_mode + per-feature toggle
from settings, not a local flag.

P4 (dispatcher loop): the handler delegates to dispatch.New(...)
.Run; the loop body, retry policy, decorator chain ordering, and
SSE writer are inherited from the foundation.

P5 (decorator chain): the dispatcher wraps the provider with the
locked decorator chain (redaction → rate limit → cost cap → audit
→ trace) installed by dispatch.Run. No per-handler decorator
reordering.

P6 (guard middleware): mountAIRoutes wraps the route with
guard.Wrap("geofence-aware-automation-suggestions", handler) so a
disabled toggle returns 404 BEFORE the handler is invoked.

P8 (eval harness): three deterministic goldens
(commute_geofence_precondition, night_charging_at_home,
refusal_other_vehicle) under the strategy package; canned mock-
provider responses match each golden by sha256-of-input. Run via
`go run ./cmd/ai-eval -feature geofence-aware-automation-suggestions`.

P9 (registry coverage): the new registry entry populates Routes
.Backend + Frontend + UITestIDs explicitly (with []string{} for
JobNames + PushKinds — no jobs / pushes). aivet pass + aigen
--check pass.

P10 (baseline coexistence): the AI surface is an additive,
opt-in panel mounted ABOVE the manual AutomationBuilder form. The
panel writes nothing; clicking "Apply to form" copies the typed
draft into the existing form state. Pressing Save still goes
through useCreateAutomationFull → POST /api/v1/automations
(canonical typed write path). The off-mode test
TestGeofenceAutomationSuggestionsAIOffManualAutomationWorks proves
the AI route returns 404 and the baseline /api/v1/automations
remains untouched.

ADR-015 §I3 baseline intact:
  - Manual AutomationBuilder + per-step editors + ConditionBuilder
    + TriggerConfigurator + ActionBuilder + Save/TestRun/Cancel
    are unchanged. Only TWO additive lines are inserted into
    AutomationBuilderPage.tsx (one import + one <FadeIn> mount).

ADR-015 §I6 404 routes:
  - Off-mode test mounts the route under guard.Wrap and asserts a
    404 response with no GUARD_BYPASSED leak in the body.

ADR-015 §I7 per-feature:
  - Both backend route AND frontend wrapper key off the same
    feature ID 'geofence-aware-automation-suggestions'.

ADR-015 §I9 redaction:
  - RedactionPolicy returns redactadapter.Wrap(redact.PolicyAlertBuilder()).
    PolicyAlertBuilder denies every PII class — vehicle, place,
    channel identifiers flow through the typed F4 envelope (the
    draft_automation_graph + validate_automation_graph tools'
    typed Args + Result), NOT through narrative prose. Geofence
    catalog injection is ID + Name + Category only — NEVER lat/lon.
    The unit test TestBuildGeofenceCatalogLine pins this.

ADR-015 §I10 type system:
  - The AI surface lives entirely under /api/v1/ai/*. No field
    on the existing baseline /api/v1/automations JSON shape is
    added or modified. The handler emits SSE only (text/event-stream).

Allowed-files deviations (precedent: slices 0036 + 0038):
  1. web/src/features/locations/** — listed in the allowed-files
     section but does NOT exist; the canonical SPA host page for
     route /automations/builder is
     web/src/features/automations/pages/AutomationBuilderPage.tsx.
     Following the slice 0036 + 0038 precedent: the AI panel is
     mounted into the actual host page even though the strict
     allowed-files glob does not list it. The W1
     wired-or-absent invariant requires real wiring, not a
     parking-lot file. Flagged here so a reviewer sees the
     deliberate deviation.
  2. web/src/ai/features.ts — auto-regenerated by `go run
     ./tools/aigen` (TS mirror of the Go registry). Touched
     unavoidably; aivet + aigen --check pass.
  3. internal/ai/redact/policies.go — NOT touched; the existing
     PolicyAlertBuilder is the prescribed policy. Reused as-is.

Tool re-use, NOT re-registration:
  - The two propose-only tools draft_automation_graph +
    validate_automation_graph are registered process-wide by
    tools.RegisterAutomationBuilderTools at router.go (called for
    slice 0016's AIAutomationHandler). Re-registering would PANIC
    on duplicate name. The new strategy lists them in allowedTools
    and the dispatcher resolves them against the SAME process-wide
    *tools.Registry. Tool implementations are stateless so
    sharing them across strategies is safe and intended.

Geofence-catalog injection design:
  - The handler loads the user's existing geofences via
    GeofenceRepo.GetAll, sorts by ID ASC for byte-stable LLM
    prompts, caps the in-prompt list at 50 entries, and emits a
    single deterministic line into the synthesised user message:
      "Geofence catalog for this user (use ONLY these place_id
       values; never invent one): [id=1 name=\"Home\" category=\"home\"], …"
    Lat/lon are NEVER emitted (PolicyAlertBuilder denies coordinate
    prose; emitting them here would either leak past the policy or
    require re-redacting the catalog line itself — defeating its
    purpose). The LLM only needs id+name+category to pick the
    right place_id; the canonical typed automation handler reads
    the geometry from the database when the saved automation runs.
  - When the catalog is empty, the handler emits a refusal hint so
    the LLM politely declines and steers the user to /geofences.

Eval-command discrepancy (documented):
  - The slice prompt says
    `make ai-eval-fast --feature geofence-aware-automation-suggestions`
    but the Makefile target does NOT accept --feature; the working
    invocation is
    `go run ./cmd/ai-eval -feature geofence-aware-automation-suggestions`
    (single dash, per slice 0038 precedent). Both forms are run in
    the GATE section; the working form is the actual proof.

